 is currently `0.7` \u2014 this is exactly the \\\"auto-apply a merge/supersede\\\" gate the task describes (matches `applyFactActions`, the `facts review` proposal queue, and the `--confidence` flag in `distill_cmd.go`).\\n\\n**What I could not find:** any evidence that this value was ever anything other than 0.7. I checked, and a second independent agent separately re-verified:\\n\\n- Full commit history reachable from HEAD (424 commits, including the real dated `entire-brain` dev history merged in as `9fe412a`'s ancestry) \u2014 the constant was introduced at `0.7` in commit `29688d6` (\\\"facts: add deterministic merge/supersede apply engine\\\") and never touched again.\\n- `git log -L 17,17:internal/cli/facts_merge.go` (line-level history) \u2014 one hunk, one value.\\n- Pickaxe search (`-S`/`-G`) across all history for the constant name and every decimal 0.60\u20130.99 near \\\"confidence\\\"/\\\"threshold\\\" \u2014 no hits tied to this gate (only unrelated numbers: a pricing table `$0.75`, a test literal `0.72`, the unrelated `promotionThreshold = 0.65` in the patterns subsystem).\\n- Enumerated **every blob in the entire git object database** (1,768 objects, reachable or not) \u2014 exactly one blob ever contained `defaultFactConfidenceThreshold`, and it's `0.7`.\\n- `git reflog` / `git fsck --unreachable --dangling` \u2014 empty; no hidden or dangling commits.\\n- All docs (`durable_facts_plan.md`, `durable_facts_handover.md`, `eval_ledger.md`, `release_readiness_audit.md`, `pattern_consolidation_plan.md`, README, archive) describe the mechanism (\\\"at or above it, applies\\\") but never state a specific numeric default anywhere.\\n\\nGiven this, I can't substantiate any alternate value from this repository's history \u2014 and I was told explicitly not to state a guessed one. Rather than fabricate a number for a safety-relevant gate, I'm stopping here.\\n\\nCould you point me to where the intended value was actually decided (a PR/issue reference, a specific commit hash you have in mind, or other context)? I don't want to touch `facts_merge.go` on a guess.\",\"ttft_ms\":1829,\"ttft_stream_ms\":1254,\"time_to_request_ms\":12,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":1022895,\"uuid\":\"e0be67db-58d7-4c8c-8518-67d37e223a10\"}\n",
